# DE C1 Medallion Pipeline — Cursor project rules

## Architecture
- Follow Bronze → Silver → Gold → Dashboard (medallion). Do not mix layer responsibilities.
- Bronze: raw ingest only. No cleaning, no dropping rows, no business transforms.
- Silver: data quality checks. FLAG bad rows; never silently delete them.
- Gold: analytics aggregations only, from Silver with documented row filters.
- Dashboard queries read Gold tables only.

## Security
- Never include secrets, API keys, passwords, tokens, or real customer PII.
- Use synthetic sample data only.

## Code
- Prefer readable, commented Python / PySpark / SQL.
- Keep Databricks Community Edition in mind (simple paths, no proprietary extras).
- Match filenames and schemas in ASSIGNMENT_PLAN.md / design docs.

## AI workflow
- Document meaningful Cursor exchanges in ai-prompts/ (prompt, response summary, accepted/changed/rejected).
- Do not invent prompt history after the fact.
